          "explanation": "Jonas et al. (JAMA 2014, 122 RCTs) found naltrexone and acamprosate both help prevent a return to drinking, yet Han et al. (JAMA Psychiatry 2021) found only about 1.6% of US adults with AUD received a medication. The tempting 'must stop first' answer is partly true for acamprosate, but naltrexone can be started while someone is still drinking, and it can be prescribed in primary care. Neither drug is addictive.",
