          "explanation": "The evidence shows near-universal exposure and some concerning associations, like the Marfella plaque study, but no proof of harm at typical levels. That supports low-cost precautions -- not heating food in plastic, filtered tap water, swapping worn items -- while keeping bigger, proven risks like smoking and radon at the top of your list. Ignoring it treats 'unproven' as 'safe'; detox supplements have no evidence; and wholesale replacement is costly for uncertain gain.",
