          "explanation": "On the impact ladder, alcohol ranks second only to smoking, and about three drinks a night raises risks for several cancers, AFib, liver disease, and poor sleep. Replacing the pan is the tempting answer because it feels concrete, but modern nonstick no longer uses PFOA and adds little exposure. Glass storage is a fine small step, and an untested whole-house filter may not target anything. Sam should also order a radon kit -- a cheap, medium-impact step.",
